        "His status in the history of Hadith and Tafsir is nearly unparalleled among the students of the Sahaba. While some later critics debated his theological leanings, the master-critics of the Golden Age, such as Sufyan al-Thawri and al-Bukhari, upheld his reliability. He spent his life as a 'Tashih' (corrector) and a traveler, moving between the Hijaz, Iraq, Egypt, and the Maghreb, spreading the pearls of wisdom he had extracted from the household of the Prophet ﷺ through his master, Ibn Abbas (RA).",
